# Architecture

Engineering OS follows a ports-and-adapters layout.

## Layers (dependency direction)

1. `interfaces/` — CLI, HTTP, dashboard. Depend on application only.
2. `application/` — use cases, orchestration, policies. Depend on `domain/` and `ports/`.
3. `domain/` + `ports/` — entities, states, value objects, Protocol contracts. No SQLite/HTTP/Podman/Cursor imports.
4. `infrastructure/` — adapters implementing ports (persistence, integrations, runtime, network, security).

Dependency arrows point inward. Domain must not import infrastructure or interfaces.

## Composition root

Construct concrete adapters only in `bootstrap.py` (or an explicit Owner/test factory). Application services receive dependencies; they do not construct GitHub, Paperclip, Podman, or Cursor clients.

## ControlPlane

`ControlPlane` is a compatibility facade. Business logic lives in focused application services / use cases. Do not grow it into a god class again.

## Packages

Prefer responsibility-oriented packages under `infrastructure/` (`persistence/`, `integrations/`, `acp/`, `runtime/`, `network/`, `security/`). Avoid `utils/`, `common/`, or `misc/` dumping grounds.

## Compatibility

Preserve public CLI commands, HTTP URLs/status codes, and SQLite schema unless the Owner explicitly authorizes a break. Prefer compatibility shims over silent renames.
